.Dd July 2, 2026
.Dt FLOPPY 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm floppy
.Nd ISA floppy disk controller and drive support
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "device floppy"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver supports NEC uPD765 and Intel 82077AA compatible floppy disk
controllers on the ISA bus.
Detected drives are published as block devices under
.Pa /dev/storage/fd0
and
.Pa /dev/storage/fd1 .
.Pp
The driver probes legacy controllers at:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li 0x3F0 / IRQ 6
primary controller
.It Li 0x370 / IRQ 10
secondary controller
.El
.Pp
Drive geometry is selected from CMOS register
.Li 0x10
for the first two drives.
Supported media profiles include 360K, 720K, 1.2M, 1.44M, and 2.88M formats.
.Pp
Transfers use ISA DMA channel 2 through a low-memory bounce buffer below
16MB.
The current implementation performs sector I/O through CHS translation and
retries failed transfers after recalibration.
.Sh BOOTABLE FLOPPY IMAGES
A bootable floppy is built by
.Pa sys/arch/i386/floppy/mkfloppy.py
from a kernel
.Ar zimage
(a setup header followed by the kernel body).
Each floppy is a 1.44M image of 2880 512-byte sectors.
Disk 1 holds a 512-byte boot sector
.Pq Pa stage1.bin ,
the real-mode loader
.Pq Pa stage2.bin ,
and as much of the kernel as fits before the end of the disk.
.Pp
A kernel too large for a single 1.44M floppy is split across several disks.
Disk 1 is filled to its end with the leading kernel sectors and the remainder
is written to companion files with a numeric suffix
.Pq Pa .2 , Pa .3 , No ... ,
each a raw kernel continuation of 2880 sectors, the last zero-padded to a
full image.
The setup image always remains on disk 1.
.Pp
At boot the loader streams the kernel to physical address 0x00100000, printing
.Dq Loading kernel
followed by one progress dot per chunk read.
When the current disk is exhausted and kernel data remains, it prints
.Dq Please insert boot disk N and press any key to continue... ,
waits for a keypress, resets the drive, and resumes reading from the first
sector of the next disk.
A kernel that fits on one floppy never prompts for a disk swap.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/dev/storage/fd0"
.It Pa /dev/storage/fd0
first floppy drive
.It Pa /dev/storage/fd1
second floppy drive
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
The driver logs controller initialization failures, recalibration failures,
and transfer status-byte decodes with the
.Li fdc:
prefix.
.Sh BUGS
Reset completion still uses a settle-delay path instead of a strict reset IRQ
handshake.
Format-track commands, disk-change detection, and full four-drive support are
not implemented yet.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ide 4 ,
.Xr scsi 4
